# base - what every machine should report: CPU, memory, disk and disk I/O,
# network, load, services, the busiest programs, and what the machine is and
# how long it has been up. See SPECIFICATION.md section 18.10 for this format.
#
# Each script's header lists what it reports. A few metrics are not on every
# platform: iowait_pct, steal_pct and busy_ms on Linux only; swap and
# inodes_used_pct on Linux and macOS; commit on Windows only; rx_drops on
# Linux and Windows.
#
# Windows has no load average, so the load job is left out there.

# The five-minute jobs each run on their own minute (cron, local time):
# disk at 1, 6, 11 and so on, diskio at 2, processes at 3, host at 4, so
# fewer runs start together. On Windows a run started with many others
# costs about twice the CPU.
#
# Copyright (c) Bankole Ogundero and the Vigil contributors
